<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osman Pazvantoğlu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1758–1807</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osman Pazvantoğlu was an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">janissary</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidin">Vidin</a> who seized control of the town around 1794 and ruled it as a rebel pasha. Opposing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selim-iii">Selim III</a>'s military reforms, he defeated government armies sent against him, backed the dahije janissaries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> and sent raiders across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and Wallachia. The sultan had to recognise him as pasha of Vidin, and he held power until his death in 1807.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osman-pazvantoglu.jpg" alt="Osman Pazvantoğlu" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osman_Pazvanto%C4%9Flu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
